<figure class="cache-figure" data-reference-path>
 <p class="figure-title">Every path ends in an accepted answer or a bounded refusal</p>
 <div class="cache-controls"><label>Request condition <select data-case><option value="warm">Valid Redis entry</option><option value="cold">Missing entry</option><option value="corrupt">Wrong tenant or schema</option><option value="outage">Redis wait exceeds budget</option><option value="busy">Redis unavailable, source full</option><option value="old">Source reply too old</option></select></label></div>
 <ol class="reference-path-stages" data-stages></ol><p class="cluster-command" data-result></p><p class="explanation" data-explanation aria-live="polite"></p>
 <figcaption>Illustrative paths through the reference application; outlined steps are active and muted steps are skipped. Each source path assumes the stated admission outcome. Shared fills and their waiter limits are examined below. This diagram neither executes a request nor claims that an elapsed client deadline cancels a sent Redis command.</figcaption>
</figure>
<script>
import{requestPaths}from'../../lib/caching/system-design.mjs';
document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-reference-path]').forEach(root=>{const select=root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-case]')!;const render=()=>{const s=requestPaths[select.value];root.querySelector('[data-stages]')!.innerHTML=s.stages.map((name,i)=>`<li class="${s.active.includes(i)?'active':''}"><span>${i+1}</span>${name}</li>`).join('');root.querySelector('[data-result]')!.textContent=s.result;root.querySelector('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=s.note;};select.onchange=render;render();});
</script>
